    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We all belong to social networks. A social network is comprised of the set of social actors and relationships among these actors. Social capital refers to the embedded resources in these social networks that an individual actor can access, build and utilize to achieve personal interests. Hence, social capital is a key determinant in our academic and career trajectories. However, social capital is not evenly distributed across individual actors. Historical and institutional processes have resulted in unequal opportunities for different social groups based on characteristics like gender and race. Fortunately, social networks are dynamic, and we can learn to recognize, nurture, and employ social capital to improve these networks.\r\n\r\nOctans seeks to empower high school students, particularly marginalized youth, by raising their awareness of the importance of social capital and guiding them to notice, act upon and expand their surrounding resources. As a web platform, Octans features (1) interactive narratives of how relevant role models have used social capital, (2) a visualization tool that helps students identify and reflect on their social networks, and (3) a goal-setting and action-planning journal with prompts and strategies to build social capital. Along with other mentoring resources, Octans aspires to prepare learners to pursue interest-driven learning pathways using their social networks.\r\n\r\nInterviews and user testing with target learners have shown that after using Octans, learners are more aware of and grateful for their social networks. Learners are better able to articulate the types of support they encounter in their social networks. Finally, they feel a greater sense of agency to work towards their goals knowing that they have the support from these bonds and the possibility of building new ones.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
